    <string name="shizuku_guide_title">Shizuku Connection Guide</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_desc">Shizuku allows XArchiver to access restricted system folders (like Android/data) without requiring root.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_connected">✅ Shizuku is currently connected and granted permission. You can browse restricted folders using the Privileged Explorer on the Home screen.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_no_permission">⚠️ Shizuku service is running, but XArchiver does not have permission.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_tap_request">Tap the \'Request Permission\' button below to authorize the app.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_how_to_start">How to start Shizuku:</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_step1">1. Install the Shizuku app from Google Play or GitHub.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_step2">2. Open Shizuku and follow the instructions to start the service (via Wireless Debugging or ADB).</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_step3">3. Once the service says \'Shizuku is running\', return here and tap \'Request Permission\'.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_step4">4. Alternatively, open the \'Privileged Explorer\' on the Home screen to trigger the permission prompt.</string>
    
